  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Necrotic Wound with only 1 creature card in graveyard (Ossuary Rats) gives Wall of Blossoms only -1/-1, making it a -1/3 which survives. The spell is completely wasted — it accomplishes nothing. Additionally, Oversold Cemetery was available to cast and would have been a strong play building toward the deck's graveyard engine.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Necrotic Wound targeting Wall of Blossoms, which only gives -1/-1 (X=1) and doesn't kill it (0/4 becomes -1/3, toughness still above 0).",
      "betterLine": "Cast Oversold Cemetery for {1}{B} to set up the graveyard recursion engine. Save Necrotic Wound for later when the graveyard has more creatures and it can actually kill a meaningful target.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 75,
      "player": "MiniMx Valley",
      "decisionIndex": 20
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Warmonger's Chariot is a do-nothing artifact that requires 3 more mana to equip before it impacts the board. Ironroot Warlord could be cast using Prophetic Prism to filter mana into white, producing an immediate 3/5 body (with Wall of Blossoms, Overgrown Battlement, and itself) that can attack next turn and has a built-in token engine. The Warlord is a much stronger tempo play.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Warmonger's Chariot for {2}",
      "betterLine": "Cast Ironroot Warlord for {1}{G}{W} using Overgrown Battlement for {G}{G}, Swamp for {B}, and Prophetic Prism to filter {B} into {W}. This puts a 3/5 attacker on board immediately.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 104,
      "player": "Gem31P Contra",
      "decisionIndex": 25
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Oversold Cemetery before playing a land drop. Should always play land before casting spells to maximize available mana. Playing Swamp first would give 4 mana total (2 remaining after Cemetery) instead of 3 mana (1 remaining after Cemetery). While no additional spells in hand could be cast with the extra mana, it leaves more open mana for flexibility.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Oversold Cemetery before playing a land",
      "betterLine": "Play Swamp first, then cast Oversold Cemetery, leaving 2 mana open instead of 1",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 110,
      "player": "MiniMx Valley",
      "decisionIndex": 26
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Gargoyle Sentinel (a 3/3 defender) when sequencing Portcullis Vine first would have increased Overgrown Battlement's mana production to 3G, enabling casting both Portcullis Vine and Ironroot Warlord in the same turn. Ironroot Warlord as a */5 (power = number of creatures, which would be 4) is a much stronger board presence than Gargoyle Sentinel, and getting both creatures down is far better than just one.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Gargoyle Sentinel for {3}",
      "betterLine": "Cast Portcullis Vine for {G} first, then tap Overgrown Battlement for 3G (now counting 3 defenders), then cast Ironroot Warlord for {1}{G}{W} using Battlement mana + remaining lands + Prophetic Prism for white. This deploys two creatures instead of one and creates a much stronger board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 130,
      "player": "Gem31P Contra",
      "decisionIndex": 32
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Portcullis Vine when it was the only available play. Portcullis Vine is a 0/3 defender that would increase Overgrown Battlement's mana production by 1 green, boost Ironroot Warlord's eventual power by 1, provide a sacrifice outlet to draw a card later, and add a blocker. There's essentially no downside to casting it.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority without casting Portcullis Vine",
      "betterLine": "Cast Portcullis Vine (using Swamp + Prophetic Prism to produce {G}) to grow the defender synergy engine and prepare for casting Ironroot Warlord next turn with more mana from Overgrown Battlement",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 136,
      "player": "Gem31P Contra",
      "decisionIndex": 33
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Passed priority in postcombat main with Portcullis Vine as a legal and beneficial cast. Portcullis Vine is a 0/3 defender that would increase Overgrown Battlement's mana production from 2 to 3 green mana (helping cast Fusion Elemental and Ironroot Warlord sooner), increase Ironroot Warlord's future power by 1, provide a body for Warmonger's Chariot, and offer a future card draw sacrifice ability. There is no downside to casting it.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without casting anything.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Portcullis Vine by tapping Swamp for {B}, using {B} to activate Prophetic Prism for {G}, then casting Portcullis Vine. This adds a defender to boost Overgrown Battlement's mana and sets up future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 140,
      "player": "Gem31P Contra",
      "decisionIndex": 34
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gravecrawler can't block, so there's zero defensive value in keeping it back. The opponent has only one untapped blocker (Wall of Blossoms 0/4). Even if Gravecrawler gets blocked and dies, it can be recast from the graveyard since MiniMx controls other Zombies (Wailing Ghoul, Suspicious Shambler). Attacking with both creatures guarantees at least one gets through since there's only one blocker.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined to attack with any creatures",
      "betterLine": "Attack with at least Gravecrawler (which can't block anyway, making it a free attack), and likely both creatures to guarantee damage gets through since the opponent has only one untapped blocker.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 152,
      "player": "MiniMx Valley",
      "decisionIndex": 39
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Attacking with Wailing Ghoul (1/3) into Gargoyle Sentinel (3/3) and Wall of Blossoms (0/4) risks losing it for no meaningful damage. The Ghoul likely gets blocked by the Sentinel and dies, accomplishing nothing except adding a creature to the graveyard (which has some Cemetery synergy, but Cemetery needs 4 creatures and there's only 1 creature card in the graveyard currently).",
      "actionTaken": "Attacked with all three creatures including Wailing Ghoul",
      "betterLine": "Attack with only Gravecrawler and Suspicious Shambler. This forces the opponent to choose which to block with Gargoyle Sentinel - either letting 2 or 4 damage through. Wailing Ghoul as a Zombie enables Gravecrawler recursion and is more valuable staying on the battlefield.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 180,
      "player": "MiniMx Valley",
      "decisionIndex": 48
    }
  ],
  "blunderScriptVersion": 32
}